# Ventus In-App Feedback licensing

This repository uses different licenses for integration components and the
self-hosted backend.

## MIT-licensed components

The following components are licensed under the MIT License in
`LICENSE-MIT.md`:

- `packages/contracts`
- `packages/api-client`
- `packages/browser`
- `packages/widget`
- `packages/react`
- `apps/mcp-server`
- `apps/demo`
- repository-level documentation, examples, scripts, and configuration, unless
  a file states otherwise

## Business Source licensed components

`apps/api` is licensed under the Business Source License 1.1 in
`LICENSE-BSL.md`, including its Additional Use Grant. Development,
non-production use, and qualifying limited production use are free. Production
use outside that grant requires a commercial license from Ventus Software
Solutions GmbH.

The BSL Additional Use Grant permits production use until the backend processes
more than 1,000 aggregate feedback submissions per calendar month for three
consecutive months. After the threshold is met, the grant provides 30 days to
obtain a commercial license or reduce usage.

This summary is informational. The license text applicable to each component
controls. A `LICENSE` file inside a component directory takes precedence over
this repository-level summary.

The MIT-licensed components are open source. The BSL-licensed backend is
source-available and is not open source before its Change Date.
